From 46e31e4f3f10c73059e4b094ab22bd3cffa6b333 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Sutton <davidhsutton@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 11:00:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] gugu: _session/steering extension method (mid-turn
 message injection)

Adds an ACP extension method with the same name and contract as
@agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp's, so clients can inject a message into
the RUNNING turn via pi's native `steer` RPC instead of waiting for the turn
boundary: injected (turn running) / promptRequired + noRunningTurn (idle,
client opted in via _meta.steering.idleBehavior) / startedNewTurn (idle).
initialize() advertises _meta.steering.supported = true.

Why: Gugu delivers group messages that arrive mid-turn this way.

Upstream: svkozak/pi-acp#115 (head d7f9cb2, cherry-picked unchanged: its two
commits squashed).

Drop when: #115 (or an equivalent) is in the upstream tag this is built on.
